[x] Inventory graphd responsibilities and freeze the compatibility baseline =graphd-inventory $Record every current producer, consumer, query artifact, output contract, build dependency, and installation path before moving code. Classify each graphd responsibility as canonical RDF publication, optional local SPARQL, client presentation, external-database concern, or deletion; capture current proving commands and bytes so retirement cannot silently drop a real capability.$ !1 ^2026-08-18T21:07 %2026-08-18T21:51 #01a01834-57fe-7b22-9d21-3d8ae9e4bdb2
[x] Specify the canonical workspace RDF dataset contract =rdf-dataset-contract $Define the publication boundary in specifications and decision history: plaintext remains authoritative; RDF is a deterministic replaceable snapshot; stable named graph and entity IRIs; supported syntaxes and datatypes; provenance and semantic reconstruction scope; no arbitrary RDF input, external mutation sync, endpoint proxy, or workspace source round-trip. Reconcile the existing ontology bridge language and identify the authoritative ontology artifacts.$ !1 ^2026-08-18T21:07 %2026-08-18T21:51 <graphd-inventory #01a01834-5811-7060-8455-ec826f879483
[x] Reconcile v4 ontology into a consistent projection arbiter =ontology-arbiter-fix $Prereq discovered while planning core-rdf-projection: ontology/v4 must be self-consistent before Core targets it. Confirmed via pyshacl that is_successor_of shapes required Plan while the projection emits successor edges between Actions (Decision 25) — real workspaces failed SHACL. Fixed in ontology repo (commit eda92bb, main): added missing Plan subClassOf Prescriptive ICE + retargeted SuccessorDomain/NoCyclicDependencies shapes to ont00000965; declared owl:inverseOf part_of<->has_part (canonical serialized direction = part_of/up); declared dcterms:description; aligned 4.3.0->4.4.0 version drift; added valid+invalid Action-chain regression fixtures. Suite 29->32 green.$ !1 ^2026-08-18T22:32 %2026-08-18T22:32 #01a01881-7402-7173-94e3-6d3d106705f9
[x] Complete v4.5.0 ontology arbiter for the RDF projection =ontology-arbiter-v450 $Made the published v4 vocabulary complete before Core consumes it, arbiter-first. Published charterState as a proper vocab term over distinct charter-lifecycle individuals CharterNew CharterActive CharterBlocked CharterClosed CharterCancelled, parallel to Action status but never sharing individuals. Recorded the single-canonical-direction policy so derivable inverses are omitted: prescribes is published, prescribed_by is not. Recorded that a plan template is not published since it has no stable identity today. Touched OWL, context, schema, shapes, and the ontology-out contract plus regression fixtures. Ontology suite 34 green. Committed and pushed as ontology c61a149.$ !1 ^2026-08-18T23:40 %2026-08-18T23:40 #01a018c0-4741-7093-a7e3-08c390a915d5
[x] Move the canonical RDF projection into Core =core-rdf-projection $Create an always-available clearhead-core rdf module using only lightweight RDF term and serialization dependencies. Move and reconcile graphd's domain-to-RDF and canonical JSON-LD logic so one dataset projection owns all triples, named graphs, stable IRIs, datatypes, deterministic ordering, validation, and every RDF serialization. JSON-LD must serialize the same canonical dataset rather than remain a parallel hand-built graph path. Keep Oxigraph, SPARQL, persistence, networking, and presentation out of Core; prove the normal dependency graph remains database-free.$ !1 ^2026-08-18T21:07 %2026-08-21T20:20 <rdf-dataset-contract #01a01834-581e-70f0-a4c7-0a499ebe4a19
[x] Make ephemeral local SPARQL an optional CLI capability =optional-sparql $CLI gains a default-on `sparql` feature — the only Oxigraph consumer (in-memory store only, no persistence). Workspace(s) -> DomainModel -> Core quads -> ephemeral store -> verbatim standard SPARQL (union default graph per specifications/ontology.md); SELECT/ASK emit SPARQL Results JSON piped / table on terminal, CONSTRUCT/DESCRIBE emit Turtle/JSON-LD. No prefix/parameter injection: saved .sparql files stay portable. Core added the pure rdf::snapshot projection (ws:Workspace identity, ws:root/charterRoot, ws:hasSourceFile/hasSourceLine from host evidence) so one Core projection still owns every published statement shape. `query raw` and locally-saved `query named` run in-process (project .clearhead/queries/ then user <config>/queries/); `--where` expands to a complete standard query. Minimal `--no-default-features` profile compiles with zero query engine and a cargo-tree gate fails if oxigraph ever enters it (pre-push + CI). graphd's built-in registry, --status injection, and the index/tree/graph/chain families keep forwarding until migrate-graph-consumers; minimal build errors cleanly on `query raw` rather than preserving the subprocess boundary for moved responsibilities. 14 CLI integration tests + Core snapshot tests; full pre-push green. clearhead-core 985ddea.$ !2 ^2026-08-18T21:07 %2026-08-21T21:35 <core-rdf-projection #01a01834-583a-7b72-ac8e-4ba1f2dfc8e5
[x] Expose whole-workspace RDF export from the CLI =cli-rdf-export $`clearhead export workspace` publishes the canonical dataset: always available (not behind the sparql feature — no engine involved), TriG default with N-Quads/JSON-LD/Turtle, dataset formats preserving each workspace's stable named graph. A new always-compiled CLI dataset module is the single load→project assembly path (workspace-fs load, Core project_domain + project_workspace_snapshot per graph, Core canonicalize merge) shared with the sparql feature's ephemeral store, so exported and queried datasets are identical; the CLI adds zero semantic mapping. Covers --workspace selection, --output files (reviewed no_naive_writes exemption, mirroring plan.rs), empty workspaces, byte-determinism, and broken pipes. Core's serializer prefix table now covers the ws: vocabulary. 9 integration tests, green in both build profiles; full pre-push green. clearhead-core 29f2a4f.$ !1 ^2026-08-18T21:07 %2026-08-21T22:05 <core-rdf-projection #01a01834-582c-7321-b77c-4986f79793b0
[x] Prove engine-independent RDF publication and queries =external-rdf-proof $The exported dataset loads into independent engines and the same saved .sparql runs unchanged. Raptor 2.0.16 parses our TriG into the exact same quad set (graph terms + canonical IRIs + typed literals preserved). rdflib 7.6.0 (independent SPARQL 1.1) returns identical results to the ClearHead in-process evaluator for 8/9 portable built-ins incl. FILTER NOT EXISTS, GROUP BY, and ORDER BY (ordered ✓). Determinism: byte-identical exports (sha256-stable). Replace-snapshot: mutation surfaces only new state in both engines; old export lacked it. Engine-local behavior recorded in docs/rdf-external-proof.md: union default graph is an evaluator convention (rdflib default_union=True / Oxigraph set_default_graph_as_union); parameterized built-ins (agenda/weekly/chain/actions-by-phase/overdue-tasks) excluded until migrate-graph-consumers; rdflib GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?opt) NotBoundError bug on all-plans (query is standard, runs in ClearHead); Rasqal 0.9.33 predates SPARQL 1.1 so rdflib is the query engine (Raptor stays the independent parser). Reproducible: bash docs/rdf-external-proof/run.sh. clearhead-core 29f2a4f, platform 982e3ef.$ !2 ^2026-08-18T21:07 %2026-08-21T22:30 <cli-rdf-export <optional-sparql #01a01834-5848-7de1-a2d0-c88bf0fe45be
